      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the values of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) given that \\(g(f(x)) = 3x + 4\\), we first need to understand the composition of the functions \\(f(x)\\) and \\(g(x)\\).\n\nGiven:\n\\[ f(x) = ax + b \\]\n\\[ g(x) = 2x - 5 \\]\n\nThe composition \\(g(f(x))\\) is:\n\\[ g(f(x)) = g(ax + b) \\]\n\nSubstituting \\(f(x)\\) into \\(g(x)\\), we get:\n\\[ g(ax + b) = 2(ax + b) - 5 \\]\n\nSimplifying the expression:\n\\[ 2(ax + b) - 5 = 2ax + 2b - 5 \\]\n\nWe are given that:\n\\[ g(f(x)) = 3x + 4 \\]\n\nEquating the two expressions:\n\\[ 2ax + 2b - 5 = 3x + 4 \\]\n\nFor the equation to hold true for all \\(x\\), the coefficients of \\(x\\) and the constant terms must be equal on both sides. Therefore, we can set up the following system of equations:\n\\[ 2a = 3 \\]\n\\[ 2b - 5 = 4 \\]\n\nFirst, solve for \\(a\\):\n\\[ 2a = 3 \\]\n\\[ a = \\frac{3}{2} \\]\n\nNext, solve for \\(b\\):\n\\[ 2b - 5 = 4 \\]\n\\[ 2b = 4 + 5 \\]\n\\[ 2b = 9 \\]\n\\[ b = \\frac{9}{2} \\]\n\nNow, find \\(a + b\\):\n\\[ a + b = \\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{9}{2} = \\frac{3 + 9}{2} = \\frac{12}{2} = 6 \\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{6}\n\\]",
